// The Mockingbird's sky: the AIR CHASE (docs/planning/game/bosses.md, "The
// Mockingbird"; Jon, 2026-10-06).
//
// An open sky that never stops moving (`sky_scroll` over the `open_sky`
// backdrop: it scrolls and wraps), framed whole on screen (its camera zone's
// zoom shows all 1280 x 720 of it). The Mockingbird holds its left side
// (`cove.mockingbird`). Three lanes of burning sharks (`MovingPlatform`
// `loop_dx`, drawn as `burning_flying_shark`, one-way: jump up through one and
// land on its back) drift toward it and wrap from the left edge back in at the
// right: the only footing. A body that falls is caught by a shark and lifted
// back into play while the Mockingbird lives (`fall_rescue`); once it is dead,
// the bottom's exit drops you to the shore below (`mockingbird_arena`), where
// its treasure fell.
//
// The side walls are invisible Solids added by `mockingbird_sky_walls.yaml`
// (a second pass: `area create` lowers static collision into IntGrid cells,
// and these must keep their transparent colour). Re-run it after every
// `area create --replace-existing`.
//
//   +----------------------------------------------+ y = 0
//   |                                              |
//   |  [Mockingbird]    <- sharks drift left       | lane 1, y 300
//   |   (home)        ===       ===       ===      | lane 2, y 430
//   |             ===       ===       ===          | lane 3, y 560
//   |                                              |
//   |============= exit: down to the shore ========| y = 704
//   +----------------------------------------------+ y = 720
(
    id: "mockingbird_sky",
    level_id: "mockingbird_sky",
    world_x: 1744,
